## Context

Surfaced at the 0446 figure review (2026-06-06): the project speaks FOUR
status vocabularies, projected into each other at different points:

1. **Reference master** (`vietnam_thermal_plants_v2_classified.csv`):
   9-class ordinal ladder — `0 exploring, 1 announced, 2 proposed,
   3 added to PDP, 4 permitted, 5 construction, 6 operating, 9 cancelled,
   10 retired`. "3 added to PDP" is Vietnam-specific (PDP inclusion is the
   national lifecycle gate), not in any internal standard.
2. **What the Exp1 prompt asks the models** (`prompt_complete.txt`):
   GEM-style 8 classes — `Announced / Pre-permit / Permitted /
   Construction / Operating / Shelved / Cancelled / Retired`.
3. **GEM standard** (Global Energy Monitor trackers): announced,
   pre-construction, permitted, construction, operating, mothballed,
   cancelled, retired, shelved — the de-facto interchange vocabulary for
   plant trackers; relevant for downstream comparability (PyPSA-VN, GEM
   reconciliation 0428/0429).
4. **Analysis + display**: the author-ratified 6-bucket v1-compat
   projection (`_STATUS_ORDINAL_PROJECTION` in evaluate.py: ordinal ≤2 →
   proposed, 3-4 → planned, 5 → constructing, 6 → operational, 9 →
   cancelled, 10 → retired) with French display labels (STATUS_LABELS in
   exp1_recognition.py) — used by the recognition matrix bands and the
   status-difficulty table; band ORDER is lifecycle since 0446.

Note the EN/FR wrinkle inside vocabulary 4: the same figure PDF serves the
French report and the English preprint (figures keep their generated
language — known limitation, cf. 0356 for slides).

## Discussion to have (imagine — no immediate action)

- Should the analysis buckets align on GEM classes (recognition scored at
  GEM granularity), or stay at the coarser ratified 6? Changing granularity
  re-touches the projection, the difficulty table, and every quoted
  recognition-by-status number — post-preprint work at the earliest.
- Should band/display labels show GEM English terms instead of (or
  alongside) the French labels, given the preprint is in English?
- Does "3 added to PDP" deserve to survive any projection (it is the
  Vietnam-specific signal a GEM mapping would erase)?
- Status is also a per-row match criterion (status_match in scoring) and a
  controlled vocabulary in the coherence scorer (_ALLOWED_STATUSES) — a
  5th and 6th place the vocabulary lives; inventory them in the same pass.

## Exit criteria (to sharpen at Plan, after discussion)

- [ ] One documented mapping table: master ordinal ↔ prompt ↔ GEM ↔
      analysis bucket ↔ display label (EN+FR), committed under docs/
- [ ] Author decision on analysis granularity and display language
- [ ] Consumers inventoried (projection, matcher, coherence vocab,
      figures, tables) with per-consumer impact of any change

